                  </h4>
                  <p className="text-sm text-amber-900/80 font-medium leading-relaxed">
                    The solver performed a full combinatorial sweep across all 24 possible start hours for both 9h (Full-Time) and 4h (Part-Time) shifts. By allowing start times to be offset (e.g. starting at 07:00 instead of being locked to the 06:00 block), the engine identified a solution that captures <strong>{Math.round(solution.weeklyStats.blendedUtilization)}%</strong> of productive capacity with only <strong>{solution.weeklyStats.wasteHours} hours</strong> of structural slack. This approach mimics a Mixed Integer Programming (MIP) model by evaluating the "Global Shadow Price" of every labor hour before assigning staff.
